---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { decks } from '../../lib/decks';
---
<Base title="OCR A-level Chemistry flashcards: key terms and definitions by topic" description="Free flashcards for OCR A-level Chemistry: the key terms and definitions for each topic, with the examiners' notes on how each is asked, spaced repetition saved in your browser, and a define-it drill from real definition questions." context="flashcards" leadLine="Know the definitions but still dropping marks on the calculations? That's what a tutor fixes.">
  <h1>Flashcards</h1>
  <p>Key terms and definitions for each topic as flip cards, with spaced repetition saved in your browser. Each card carries what the examiners say about how the term is asked and marked. Definitions are the cheapest marks on the paper, and OCR's mark schemes want the exact wording: every phrase in bold on the card earns part of the mark. Decks for the remaining topics are being written; the <a href="/practice/define/">define-it drill</a> already covers every real definition question.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Terms</th><th>Drill</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{decks.map((d) => <tr><td><a href={`/questions/${d.topic}/`}>{d.name}</a></td><td><a href={`/questions/${d.topic}/terms/`}>{d.terms.length} terms</a></td><td><a href="/practice/define/">Define it</a></td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h2>How to use them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Say the answer out loud before you flip. Then be honest with "Knew it" or "Didn't know it": the cards you miss come back every round, the ones you know come back less often.</li>
    <li>A definition that would score full marks in the exam is the target: the term's meaning in one precise sentence, with the quantity (one mole, gaseous atoms, standard conditions) where that is part of the definition.</li>
    <li>"Print all" on any deck gives you paper cards.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
